{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418179-fire-and-water-engines-or-steam-engines","id":1418179,"title":"Fire and Water Engines (or Steam Engines)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-14T05:37:36-07:00","id":1418179,"title":"Fire and Water Engines (or Steam Engines)","content":"Ranges from Artifact 2 to 3, differing in size and strength. <br /> <br /> The victory of the primordials was a time of great change. Like people who have been in a dark cave all their lives, and then for the first time, saw the light. Humanity, for the first time was free. Free to do its own thing. Free to innovate by itself. Not all of them were in mud huts. Some were slaves of primordial races or lived in heaven as pets or worked for the Dragon Kings. After Humanity obtained their own independence, they sought to make their own independent culture and technology, with the Exalted blazing a trail through. Not for them the glowing artifacts of the Jadeborn, the crystal and plant technology of the Dragon Kings, or the living creatures of the Lintha. Instead they would use something else. A famed Dragonblooded artisan whose name is lost to time created the Fire and Water Engines, observing the way water would vaporize upon contact with hot stones.<br /> <br /> The Fire and Water Engines are composed out of jadesteel, fire and black jade, with a fire and water elemental bound within them, not unlike those anvils which can heat up using a fire elemental bound within it. Unlike the fire anvil, the elementals in engines are there permanently, and are specialized to work when properly propiated with incense, sacred oils, blood, music, or even prayer. Fire and Water Engines were used to pump water, to drive mills, to propel the early jade-steel hulled ships, to work the early forges, and great trains that propelled themselves through the wilderness as the Exalted slowly entrenched their power within Creation proper. <br /> <br /> As time passed and the Exalted advanced forward, such artifacts came out of fashion. They worked well enough, and required only mortals to run. And yet they were clunky, noisy, inelegant, and required maintenance after a fashion. Replaced by engines that were the embodiment of unstoppable movement, elegant golems, or other more esoteric engines, they no longer favored. And so they were decommissioned, engines great and small taken from their places of work, either broken down to be recycled or simply placed within museums, hulks rusting in warehouses or in the exhibits as the rare visitors gazed upon a long-obsolete piece of technology. The Shogunate took these rusted out hulks and gave them new life, their ease of construction and maintenance meaning they were used en masse in the great rail roads of the time, replacing the teleport gates. In this day and age, few are left, ravaged by Fair Folk incursions, the passage of time, and Lunar guerilla warfare. <br /> <br /> Nowadays the majority of such artifacts are now within the Realm and Lookshy*, the rare few within the Threshold, and in long defunct warehouses that nobody has bothered to dig up. If someone *does* dig them up, then it could rewarp the entirety political system for miles. The artifacts are not easy for mortals to make, but they *are* easy to run, and have uses for industry. They can be used to replace windmills and water wheels, be able to work pumps and bellows, work great irrigation channels or even move tremendously large vehicles, like paddleships, war machines, or caravan trailer. <br /> <br /> <br /> *Yes, this mean you can fight on train cars when your Solars invade the Realm. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64